# Mirrorweave makes each other creature a copy of its target until end of turn (CR 707.2): a token included, which stays a
# token. Its target is Frenzied Trapbreaker, Outland Liberator transformed at night: its copiable values are that face's
# (CR 707.8), those of a double-faced permanent - which only a token made as a copy of them would take both faces from
# (CR 707.8a). Fable of the Mirror-Breaker's Goblin Shaman token becomes a 3/3 Frenzied Trapbreaker with nightbound, a copy
# effect over it like any creature's, and is a 2/2 Goblin Shaman again as the turn ends (CR 514.2).
#
# Turn 1: Plains, Mox Ruby, Black Lotus for Fable (a Goblin Shaman token); Mox Emerald, then Outland Liberator from the
# Emerald and the Ruby (it becomes day, CR 702.145d). Bot2 casts nothing on turn 2, so turn 3 is night (CR 731.2) and the
# Liberator becomes Frenzied Trapbreaker. Turn 3: Fable's chapter II (nothing discarded), a Plains, and Mirrorweave on the
# Trapbreaker from both Plains, the Emerald and the Ruby.

